{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-23448",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "APM Server vulnerable to Insertion of Sensitive Information into Log File"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered whereby APM Server could log at ERROR level, a response from Elasticsearch indicating that indexing the document failed and that response would contain parts of the original document. Depending on the nature of the document that the APM Server attempted to ingest, this could lead to the insertion of sensitive or private information in the APM Server logs."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-23448",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-23448\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/elastic/apm-server\nFixed Version: 8.12.1\nLink: [CVE-2024-23448](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-23448)\nAn issue was discovered whereby APM Server could log at ERROR level, a response from Elasticsearch indicating that indexing the document failed and that response would contain parts of the original document. Depending on the nature of the document that the APM Server attempted to ingest, this could lead to the insertion of sensitive or private information in the APM Server logs.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-23448**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/elastic/apm-server|8.12.1|[CVE-2024-23448](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-23448)|\n\nAn issue was discovered whereby APM Server could log at ERROR level, a response from Elasticsearch indicating that indexing the document failed and that response would contain parts of the original document. Depending on the nature of the document that the APM Server attempted to ingest, this could lead to the insertion of sensitive or private information in the APM Server logs."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.7,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 7.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.7",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-37286",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "APM Server vulnerable to Insertion of Sensitive Information into Log File"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "APM server logs contain document body from a partially failed bulk index request. For example, in case of unavailable_shards_exception for a specific document, since the ES response line contains the document body, and that APM server logs the ES response line on error, the document is effectively logged."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-37286",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-37286\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/elastic/apm-server\nFixed Version: 8.14.0\nLink: [CVE-2024-37286](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-37286)\nAPM server logs contain document body from a partially failed bulk index request. For example, in case of unavailable_shards_exception for a specific document, since the ES response line contains the document body, and that APM server logs the ES response line on error, the document is effectively logged.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-37286**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/elastic/apm-server|8.14.0|[CVE-2024-37286](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-37286)|\n\nAPM server logs contain document body from a partially failed bulk index request. For example, in case of unavailable_shards_exception for a specific document, since the ES response line contains the document body, and that APM server logs the ES response line on error, the document is effectively logged."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.7,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 6.9,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.7",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39828",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: Unauthorized command execution via discarded SSH permissions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When an SSH server authentication callback returned PartialSuccessError with non-nil Permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. Returning non-nil Permissions with PartialSuccessError now results in a connection error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39828",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39828\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: 0.52.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-39828](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39828)\nWhen an SSH server authentication callback returned PartialSuccessError with non-nil Permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. Returning non-nil Permissions with PartialSuccessError now results in a connection error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39828**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|golang.org/x/crypto|0.52.0|[CVE-2026-39828](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39828)|\n\nWhen an SSH server authentication callback returned PartialSuccessError with non-nil Permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. Returning non-nil Permissions with PartialSuccessError now results in a connection error."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
